* Reference 1.2.1: an identifier is a string of alphanumeric characters
* beginning with an uppercase letter, and its length must not exceed 15
* characters. `ThisNameIsSeventeen` is 17, so it is not an identifier and the
* lexer must say so rather than truncate it.
$ENTRY Go {
  = <ThisNameIsSeventeen>;
}

ThisNameIsSeventeen {
  = ;
}
